---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About the library" section="About"
  ><div class="reading-heading">
    <span class="eyebrow">KNOWLEDGE THAT STAYS WITH YOU</span><h1>
      A learning record,<br />built one shift at a time.
    </h1><p class="lead">
      Fieldnotes connects veterinary knowledge to the conversations and experiences it came from.
    </p><div class="prose">
      <h2>From a conversation to a connected library</h2><p>
        Authorized recordings can become timestamped transcripts, detailed discussions, clinical
        case records, and source-linked knowledge articles. Repeated topics improve existing
        articles while individual discussions remain accessible.
      </p><h2>Keep the evidence visible</h2><p>
        Owner reports, direct observations, clinical suspicions, confirmed diagnoses, actual
        actions, proposed treatments, and educational explanations have distinct labels. Missing
        details remain unknown.
      </p><h2>A private process, a reviewed public library</h2><p>
        Processing and public publication are separate. Only content approved for public release
        belongs on this website. Review includes authorization and confidentiality; removing names
        alone is insufficient.
      </p><h2>Study without an account</h2><p>
        Study questions are prepared ahead of time. No model is called when you answer. Your session
        stays in this page’s memory and is discarded when you leave. No performance history is
        stored.
      </p><h2>Current development</h2><p>
        The production library begins empty. An independent synthetic dataset demonstrates all
        sections during development. Clinical examples in demonstration mode are fictional, and
        equipment observations are not validated operating instructions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div></Layout
>
